n","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:a57f6446526ad7b153f1a23b3cf8a90875d21074301ac497345b49a2cf4a81c7","file":"preprints/quasi-isometric-recognition-of-virtually-polycyclic-groups-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex","line":95,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"1e8e39c574e7cc3ced50a0216c42bb4907117d75cbe610fe1b1379973982ca82","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/quasi-isometric-recognition-of-virtually-polycyclic-groups-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:a57f6446526ad7b153f1a23b3cf8a90875d21074301ac497345b49a2cf4a81c7","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/quasi-isometric-recognition-of-virtually-polycyclic-groups-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex#L95"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:bounded-height}\nLet $G$ be a connected simply connected real-triangulable unimodular Lie group, with a fixed left invariant Riemannian metric, exponential height map $\\pi:G\\to W$, and a fixed norm on $W$. There is a finite subgroup $\\A_G\\leq\\GL(W)$ such that, for every $K\\geq1$ and $C\\geq0$, there is a constant $B=B(G,K,C)$ with the following property. Every $(K,C)$ self quasi-isometry $F$ of $G$ has an $A_F\\in\\A_G$ satisfying\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:height-main}\n \\bigl\\|\\pi F(g)-\\pi F(1)-A_F\\pi(g)\\bigr\\|\\leq B\n \\qquad(g\\in G).\n\\end{equation}"}
